# Status page design system

Before creating or modifying status-page markup or styles:

1. Read `docs/DESIGN.md`.
2. Read `docs/DESIGN_BRIEF.md` for who the page is for.
3. Read `docs/DESIGN_DECISIONS.md` before changing layout, color, type, or motion.
4. Reuse the signal, row, incident, and footer patterns in `docs/COMPONENT_GUIDELINES.md` and `src/status/render.ts`.
5. Change tokens in `src/status/pageCss.ts`. Do not add a second stylesheet, Tailwind, or a font CDN.
6. Keep text in `--ink` or `--muted` on `--sheet`. Status color is a lamp or a row strip, and the status word is always present.
7. Keep the page usable at 640px and below. Keep the focus outline on links.
8. Do not introduce the generic patterns listed in `docs/DESIGN.md`: cream and terracotta, acid green on black, rounded card grids, soft shadows, all-caps eyebrows, middle-dot meta, or load animations.
9. After a visual change, load `GET /status/:slug` in a browser at a wide viewport and at a narrow one.
10. Preserve the JSON status document, the heading `Dependencies`, component display names, the badge status word, and `Automatic:` in the Atom feed.
11. When the design system changes, update `docs/DESIGN.md` and `docs/DESIGN_DECISIONS.md` in the same change.
